        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;For months now, the United States has been destroying boats in the Caribbean Sea and Pacific Ocean, killing everyone onboard. They claim that these boats are being used to smuggle drugs into the United States, but have yet to provide any evidence that any of the people they&#39;ve killed were actually smuggling drugs. Now, the regime is ordering the U.S. military to invade Latin America by land to expand its indiscriminate killing spree even further.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;There&#39;s no question that the United States has a major drug problem. But there&#39;s also no evidence that killing hundreds of people without any judicial process has done or will do anything to address that problem. Instead, this is just an excuse for the Trump regime to bully countries in Central and South America into ceding their autonomy to the United States. Trump campaigned on putting America First, and has instead spent his entire second term in office violating international law and pushing American involvement in countries around the world while letting the United States fall into economic and political turmoil.&lt;/p&gt;
