&lt;section&gt;
    &lt;p class=&quot;tangerine&quot; style=&quot;text-align:center;font-size:4em;padding:1.2rem 0px;&quot;&gt;Impeach. Convict. Remove.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Recap of this week in the revolution: Mitch McConnell&amp;#39;s pre-obituary. Trump withholds $1 billion in Medicaid payments and announces new round of illegal tariffs. Trump Media wants to charge for social media posts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-good&quot;&gt;
	&lt;h4&gt;The good...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Kentucky columnist publishes &quot;pre-obituary&quot; of missing Senator Mitch McConnell &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.newsweek.com/mcconnell-faces-scathing-pre-death-obituary-in-largest-home-state-newspaper-12234670&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/xzrelmz-_h-484.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Mitch McConnell is the best metaphor of American politics. He spent 41 years making the world a better place for only himself and his friends, married an immigrant while working tirelessly against other immigrants, manipulated the system to increase his power only to be usurped and made impotent by someone even MORE unethical and power hungry. Then when the system is finally done with him, his party keeps his limp body on life support just to use him for one more power move, while his wife flees the country and his children go into hiding. And when it&#39;s all said and done, he&#39;ll be best remembered for that meme that made him into a turtle.&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/xzrelmz-_h-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;484&quot; height=&quot;672&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/xzrelmz-_h-200.webp 200w, /images/xzrelmz-_h-484.webp 484w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Senator Mitch McConnell.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;Columnist Joseph Gerth wrote a &quot;pre-obituary&quot; for Senator Mitch McConnell for the &lt;i&gt;Louisville Courier Journal,&lt;/i&gt; Kentucky&#39;s largest newspaper.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;Gerth blasts McConnell for blocking the appointment of Obama&#39;s nomination of Merrick Garland to the Supreme Court in March of 2016, arguing that because it was an election year, the nomination should fall to whoever won the November election and took office in 2017. But after the death of Ruth Bader Ginsburg in 2020 (also an election year), McConnell pushed the nomination of Amy Coney Barrett to the Supreme Court so she could be quickly confirmed before the Joe Biden took office.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;blockquote&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;With McConnell allegedly on the mend, I figured I&#39;d go ahead and tell you what I think about McConnell now, when no one can complain, &#39;How dare you write that about a dead guy?&#39;&lt;br/&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;His biggest failing may be his embrace of a president who he believes is stupid and who he believes led an attempt to overthrow the United States&#39; government on Jan. 6, 2021.&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;figcaption class=&quot;blockquote-footer&quot;&gt;Joseph Gerth, &lt;i&gt;Louisville Courier Journal&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;
        &lt;/blockquote&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;Senator McConnell has not been seen publicly or performed his duties as a Senator since he was hospitalized on June 14. The lack of transparency about the senator&#39;s condition and prognosis has raised concerns. If McConnell is deceased or unable to carry out his duties, the state is required to hold an election to replace him in the Senate through the end of his current term (January, 2027). The general consensus is that the Republican Party is concealing McConnell&#39;s actual condition in hopes of avoiding triggering that special election. If the special election does not happen by August 3, 2026, there will be no special election and the seat will just remain empty until January.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;According to Kentucky state law, the governor is not able to appoint a replacement for a vacant Senate seat, which is what happened when South Carolina Senator Lindsey Graham died recently and Governor Henry McMaster appointed his sister, Darline Graham Nordone to replace him.&lt;/p&gt;

        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
