                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.courier-journal.com/story/opinion/columnists/gerth/2026/07/22/senator-mitch-mcconnell-lindsay-graham-trump-voting-rights-act-supreme-court-republican-party/90981848007/?gnt-cfr=1&amp;gca-cat=p&amp;gca-uir=true&amp;gca-epti=undefined&amp;gca-ft=0&amp;gca-ds=sophi&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-lock&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Louisville Courier Journal) Gerth: My too-early &quot;tribute&quot; to Mitch McConnell | Opinion&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-bad&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The bad...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Trump regime withholds $1 billion in Medicaid payments to California and Minnesota &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/medicaid-fraud-minnesota-california-oz-rfk-trump-24033ef9807b46f8b6fd6614ef5b1169&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/h5Ecg63HD--800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Wealthy vs poor&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/h5Ecg63HD--200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;990&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/h5Ecg63HD--200.webp 200w, /images/h5Ecg63HD--800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;Image by &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com/users/prettysleepy-2973588/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=5307356&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amy&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com//?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=5307356&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Pixabay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;The Trump regime is refusing to pay more than $1 billion in Medicaid payments to California and Minnesota as punishment for &lt;i&gt;suspected&lt;/i&gt; fraud and noncompliance. Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. said that it makes more sense to punish these states on the mere suspicion of wrongdoing rather than going through the tedious process of proving their guilt &lt;i&gt;before&lt;/i&gt; they are sentenced.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;The move is an attempt to fool Americans into believing that the regime is cracking down on fraud to save taxpayers&#39; money. Meanwhile, Trump&#39;s unpopular and illegal war with Iran rages on unchecked at a cost to taxpayers of over $37 billion to date with no end in sight. As usual, the government hasn&#39;t provided any &quot;data or explanation on how the deferral amount was calculated or what it was based on,&quot; according to John Connolly, Minnesota&#39;s state Medicaid director.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/medicaid-fraud-minnesota-california-oz-rfk-trump-24033ef9807b46f8b6fd6614ef5b1169&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(AP) Trump administration says it&#39;s deferring $1B in Medicaid payments to California and Minnesota&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        President TACO&#39;s latest tariff announcements &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/trump-tariffs-supreme-court-forced-labor-4ea091eeee3fa1bfbe55af3f482e6bc1&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/NxScXcMnTh-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Trump&#39;s &#39;Liberation Day&#39; tariff chart, 2025&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/NxScXcMnTh-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;601&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/NxScXcMnTh-200.webp 200w, /images/NxScXcMnTh-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Trump&#39;s &quot;Liberation Day&quot; tariff chart, April 2, 2025.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Donny 2-Dolls is announcing a new wave of tariffs to be levied on imports from dozens of countries. The Supreme Court ruled that his last round of tariffs were illegal, but Trump has never been one to stop doing a thing just because it&#39;s against the law.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;The new tariffs will affect around 99% of all U.S. imports. The first round of tariffs were issued under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA), which gives the president power to respond to emergencies. Trump declared that it was an emergency that the United States imports more goods than it exports, and under that justification imposed tariffs on most of our trading partners around the world. The Supreme Court ruled that there was no emergency, and thus Trump&#39;s tariffs were illegal. In response, Trump imposed a temporary tariff of 10% on all global trade under the Trade Act of 1974. This Act is also intended to allow the president to respond to emergencies, and was also viewed as illegal. The temporary tariffs and will be expiring right as his third attempt at imposing global tariffs&amp;mdash;estimated to cost Americans more than $100 billion a year&amp;mdash; go into effect.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/trump-tariffs-supreme-court-forced-labor-4ea091eeee3fa1bfbe55af3f482e6bc1&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(AP) Trump imposes double-digit tariffs on dozens of countries as his 10% levies are set to expire Friday&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-ugly&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The ugly...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Grifter in Chief now wants investors and media companies to pay $100,000 a month to be the first to read his free social media posts &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/18/trump-media-reportedly-mulling-fee-for-first-access-to-social-media-posts&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/qX7CAnE-Qi-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Victorian-style image of a pig in fancy clothing&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/qX7CAnE-Qi-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;800&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/qX7CAnE-Qi-200.webp 200w, /images/qX7CAnE-Qi-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;Image by &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com/users/deeznutz1-3086161/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=8220398&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Dee&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com//?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=8220398&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Pixabay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Donny 2-Dolls&#39; media company is considering charging $100,000 a month to financial traders and firms who want to be the first to read his social media posts. But don&#39;t worry if that&#39;s too much for your budget, because they are also offering a discounted tier for the low, low price of $60,000 a month if you sign up for a three-year plan.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;This proposal should be seen as confirmation that Trump is using his presidency to benefit himself and his supporters financially. The only reason anyone would pay for early access to the rantings of this decrepit old man is because his posts have a direct and measurable affect on the U.S. market. Trump routinely uses social media to announce his official policies, so early access to this information will allow investors to anticipate the stock market&#39;s reaction to such policies, or to place bets on prediction markets using insider information that is not yet publicly available.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;blockquote&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;He’s selling expedited, privileged access to information about what he is doing as president.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;It’s yet more brazen corruption, an improper exploitation of government power to enrich himself.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;figcaption class=&quot;blockquote-footer&quot;&gt;Kathleen Clark, Washington University School of Law&lt;/figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/blockquote&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/18/trump-media-reportedly-mulling-fee-for-first-access-to-social-media-posts&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(Al Jazeera) Trump Media reportedly mulling fee for first access to social media posts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
