&lt;section class=&quot;block the-good&quot;&gt;
	&lt;h4&gt;The good...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Secret Handshake installs &quot;Operation Epic Furious&quot; video game on the National Mall &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.the-independent.com/news/world/americas/us-politics/trump-iran-war-arcade-game-secret-handshake-b2974563.html&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/S5j12PFBK0-630.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Operation Epic Furious: Strait to Hell&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/S5j12PFBK0-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;630&quot; height=&quot;435&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/S5j12PFBK0-200.webp 200w, /images/S5j12PFBK0-630.webp 630w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Operation Epic Furious: Strait to Hell&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Secret Handshake, the group behind the statues that have appeared in Washington D.C. depicting Trump and Epstein in various friendly poses, has placed an arcade-style game called &quot;Operation Epic Furious: Strait to Hell&quot; on the National Mall. The game is a mockery of the entire Trump regime, featuring Donny 2-Dolls himself, of course, along with J.D. Vance, Kash Patel, Pete Hegseth, Robert F. Kennedy Jr., Elon Musk, and several other prominent members of the regime. In the game, Trump is trying to collect all the oil in Iran by fighting enemies such as Iranian schoolgirls, the Pope, and low-flow showerheads.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Can&#39;t make it to the National Mall? Don&#39;t worry, the game is also available &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicfurious.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;online&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.the-independent.com/news/world/americas/us-politics/trump-iran-war-arcade-game-secret-handshake-b2974563.html&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(The Independent) Group behind Trump-Epstein statue has a new DC monument - an arcade game that makes fun of the president&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicfurious.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Play &lt;i&gt;Operation Epic Furious: Strait to Hell&lt;/i&gt; online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-bad&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The bad...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Trump exempts biggest polluters from air quality regulations &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.propublica.org/article/clean-air-act-exemptions-trump-emails&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/etsO6UWaxI-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Donny 2-Dolls&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/etsO6UWaxI-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;1000&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/etsO6UWaxI-200.webp 200w, /images/etsO6UWaxI-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Donny 2-Dolls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Since last year, Trump has been granting requests to waive the Clean Air Act to any company that asks him to. So far, 180 facilities, many of whom have already been cited for violations of the Act, have been given a two-year exemption from all Clean Air Act regulations. An estimated 250,000 people live within a mile of one of these facilities, and now face potential health risks as these companies can suddenly ignore the very regulations that were put into place to protect the lives and health of Americans.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;These exemptions are granted by Donny 2-Dolls without seeking any input from EPA scientists or consulting any legal experts, environmental groups, or the American people. This is part of a broader pattern in which the Trump regime is destroying all of the progress this country has made in clean energy and environmental protection over the past 50 years. &lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;blockquote&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;In order to help the rich get richer, he’s deregulating everything.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;He’s a tyrant. He disregards the checks-and-balances system. He overreaches through executive dictates.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;figcaption class=&quot;blockquote-footer&quot;&gt;Eduardo Sanchez, Arizona resident living near a massive copper mining and smelting operation&lt;/figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/blockquote&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.propublica.org/article/clean-air-act-exemptions-trump-emails&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(ProPublica) Trump exempted some of the nation&#39;s biggest polluters from air quality rules. All it took was an email.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Trump regime says conservation is not a valid use of public lands &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/trump-public-lands-conservation-rule-4fbe822476225ac525e185b0c74c13c1&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/CcAPaQrxOI-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;AI generated oil pump in the rain&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/CcAPaQrxOI-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;456&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/CcAPaQrxOI-200.webp 200w, /images/CcAPaQrxOI-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;Image by &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com/users/izhar-ahamed-10039532/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=9006822&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;izhar ahamed&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com//?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=9006822&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Pixabay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;The Trump regime is rolling back a rule that declares that &quot;conservation&quot; and &quot;development&quot; of public lands should be treated as equally valid uses. The U.S. Bureau of Land Management oversees about 10% of land in the U.S., and allows land to be leased for legitimate uses, which used to include conservation or restoration efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;This regime has been hell-bent on turning our nation&#39;s precious public lands into fossil fuel production sites that allow private oil companies to profit of of taxpayer-owned lands.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/trump-public-lands-conservation-rule-4fbe822476225ac525e185b0c74c13c1&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(AP) Trump administration cancels rule that made conservation a use of public lands&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-ugly&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The ugly...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Trump wants to give January 6 insurrectionists a payout &lt;a href=&quot;https://abcnews.com/US/trump-poised-drop-irs-suit-launch-17b-weaponization/story?id=132962661&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/KfKky0V1DM-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Protesters attack Capital Police during January 6 insurrection in 2021&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/KfKky0V1DM-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;450&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/KfKky0V1DM-200.webp 200w, /images/KfKky0V1DM-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Protesters attack Capital Police during January 6 insurrection in 2021&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;One of the first executive orders Donny 2-Dolls passed on his first day of his second term offered blanket pardons for 1,500 violent insurrectionists who had been charged with and were being tried for or had been convicted of criminal charges in their attempt to overthrow our democracy on January 6, 2021.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Apparently, that&#39;s not enough for him. Now he&#39;s planning to spend $1.7 billion of the taxpayers&#39; money to hand out at his discretion to anyone who he feels were unfairly treated. On the outside, the fund is being set up to settle claims brought by those who allege that they were harmed by their charges, trials, and/or convictions. But under the hood, Trump will have complete authority to appoint or remove members of the commission responsible for paying the funds, and the details of or reasons for the payouts would not be disclosed to the public.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://abcnews.com/US/trump-poised-drop-irs-suit-launch-17b-weaponization/story?id=132962661&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(ABC) Trump poised to drop IRS suit, launch $1.7B &quot;weaponization&quot; fund for allies: Sources&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;


