        This week in the Gerrymandering War of 2026
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/99zuu3Gmaj-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Gerrymandering War of 2026&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/99zuu3Gmaj-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;598&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/99zuu3Gmaj-200.webp 200w, /images/99zuu3Gmaj-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;The U.S. Supreme Court overturned an order for Alabama to use it&#39;s current court-mandated U.S. House district map until after the 2030 census. This freed up the state to redraw its maps to erase this district and gain an extra Republican seat in the house in 2026. Alabama will reschedule it&#39;s primary elections so that they can put the new map in place before the primaries take place.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;South Carolina was unable to pass a measure to allow them to redraw their map to eliminate the only Democratic-held seat in the state, but is likely to try again to push through a new map before their primaries take place in June.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Missouri redrew their maps last year, but the new maps were challenged until this week, when the State Supreme Court ruled that the maps met the state&#39;s criteria and could be used despite the fact that the new maps do not reflect the wishes of voters in the state.&lt;/p&gt;
